    "why2": "Confusing parallelization with orchestrator-workers. In parallelization the split is predefined in code; in orchestrator-workers an LLM decides the subtasks dynamically.",
    "deep": "'Building effective agents' lists the same patterns plus orchestrator-workers. It notes prompt chaining can add programmatic 'gates' between steps and trades latency for accuracy; routing can send easy queries to smaller models and hard ones to more capable models; parallelization comes as sectioning (independent subtasks) or voting (same task several times for confidence); orchestrator-workers suits tasks where subtasks cannot be predicted, such as multi-file code changes; evaluator-optimizer fits when evaluation criteria are clear and iteration measurably helps. (Source: https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/building-effective-agents)"
