    "why": "The entry point should follow the user and the work, not precede them. On the exam, the first question to ask of any option is: who is the user, and does this wrapper fit them?",
    "why2": "Choosing a custom build for a non-technical team with no integration requirement. If no programmatic access is needed, a ready-made product with Projects is faster and cheaper.",
    "deep": "Claude Code docs confirm the surfaces: terminal CLI, VS Code and JetBrains extensions, a desktop app, and the web at claude.ai/code, all connected to the same engine so CLAUDE.md files, settings and MCP servers work across them; it also integrates with GitHub Actions and GitLab CI/CD, Slack, and Chrome. (Source: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/overview)",
