     "Some entry-point decisions are not at your discretion. When a partner is subject to attorney-client privilege, HIPAA, GDPR, FedRAMP or an internal data-residency policy, those constraints rule options in or out before cost, ergonomics or build effort enter the conversation. Name the governing constraint when you recommend an entry point and let it eliminate options before preferences do.",
     "Claude.ai is the entry point this hits most often: the consumer product was not designed to satisfy every enterprise data-handling requirement out of the box. The API or SDK, routed through a partner-approved gateway with logging, retention and identity controls in the partner's own infrastructure, is what survives most regulated reviews.",
     "HIPAA turns on BAA coverage of the specific configuration in use: a BAA for one configuration does not extend to another, and beta features are generally excluded unless explicitly listed as eligible. For government work the course lists Claude for Government for FedRAMP High civilian workloads, Bedrock GovCloud for FedRAMP High and DoD IL4/5, and Vertex Assured Workloads for FedRAMP High and IL2, noting that authorized environments receive new models after commercial release. Always verify current authorization scope with Anthropic before committing."
