    "id": "p2e",
    "title": "Prompt engineering techniques across models",
    "intro": "Inside a well-designed prompt, the technique is chosen by task complexity, not habit — and the prompt-model pairing is what you actually ship.",
    "recap": "Start zero-shot, add examples when format or judgment is easier to show than tell, and add reasoning when the path matters. Claude-specific practices (clear and direct, motivation, XML tags, long documents first, thinking instead of manual CoT on newer models) and bias controls apply on top, and every technique must be re-validated when the model changes."
