    "id": "pf3-embeddings",
    "part": "p3c",
    "h": "Choosing an embedding model",
    "p": [
     "Anthropic does not offer its own embedding model. The official embeddings page points to Voyage AI as one provider with a wide range of models, while advising you to assess several vendors for your use case. This is a classic exam trap: a design that says 'use Claude's embeddings endpoint' is wrong.",
     "The docs list three selection criteria. **Dataset size and domain specificity**: models trained on larger or more domain-relevant data produce better in-domain embeddings. **Inference performance**: embedding lookup speed and end-to-end latency, especially important at large production scale. **Customization**: options to continue training on private data or specialize for unique vocabularies. Voyage's catalog illustrates the trade space with general-purpose, latency-optimized, and code-specialized models, plus rerankers.",
     "Embed queries and documents with the right mode. Voyage's API distinguishes `input_type=\"document\"` for corpus chunks from `input_type=\"query\"` for the incoming question; mixing them up degrades similarity. And changing the embedding model means re-embedding the corpus, so treat the model as a versioned dependency with a migration plan, not a setting you flip.",
     "Embedding choice is one input to retrieval quality, not the only one. If exact identifiers are being missed, a better embedding model will not fix it; a sparse index will."
    ],
    "why": "Knowing that embeddings come from a third-party provider changes the integration diagram: another vendor, another data-processing agreement, and another component to monitor.",
    "why2": "Switching embedding models to fix exact-match failures, or changing models without re-embedding the existing index.",
    "deep": "'Anthropic does not offer its own embedding model' and the three selection criteria are quoted from the official page, which lists current Voyage models, multimodal and contextualized-chunk models, and the rerank-3 reranker. (Source: https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/embeddings)",
