    "why": "Scenarios may describe a suite that is 100% passing and ask why it isn't telling the team anything. A saturated suite still catches regressions but gives no signal for improvement — you need capability evals with headroom.",
    "why2": "Running each eval case once and treating pass/fail as definitive. With probabilistic outputs, a single pass can be luck; measure success rate across trials.",
    "deep": "Anthropic's agent-eval article defines capability evals ('a hill to climb') versus regression evals (near 100%), pass@k versus pass^k, eval saturation, and the trade-offs of automated evals, production monitoring, A/B testing, user feedback, manual transcript review and systematic human studies, recommending a combination. (Source: https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/demystifying-evals-for-ai-agents)",
