    "why2": "Assuming the model itself is 'FedRAMP authorized' or 'HIPAA compliant'. Authorizations attach to environments and agreements, and compliance depends on how you configure and use them.",
    "deep": "Public-sector FAQ: FedRAMP and DoD Impact Levels certify cloud services, not AI models; models run inside authorized environments and customers maintain compliance through the hosting platform. Claude for Government does not yet include Claude Code or Cowork; government customers needing a FedRAMP environment for Claude Code can use Bedrock or Vertex. Course note: the source and the docs consulted did not cover the EU AI Act, so it is not mapped here. (Sources: https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13756069-public-sector-faqs ; https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13296973-hipaa-ready-enterprise-plans)",
