    "id": "pf5-key-takeaways",
    "part": "p5-tk",
    "h": "Module key takeaways",
    "p": [
     "1. **Safety is a stack of layers, not a setting.** Training reduces broad harm for every request but never saw your partner's domain policy, data rules or authorization model. Draw the boundary explicitly and name the layer that enforces each rule; the dangerous failure is silent, assuming Claude enforces a rule that lives in no layer.",
     "2. **Assess risk as a written deliverable.** Walk user input, retrieved content, tool outputs, model output and logs; cover injection (direct and indirect), token exhaustion, tool abuse, data exposure, hallucination, leak, bias, distribution shift and cascading failure; record likelihood, impact, control, owner and evidence.",
     "3. **A guarded path has three control points and a chosen failure direction.** Input screening, output screening and tool-call authorization answer different questions, so one filter at the end does not cover the others. Chain model-based and deterministic checks, make authorization deterministic, screen retrieved and tool content, and fail closed where a wrong pass causes harm. Audit skills before trust and confine them at runtime.",
     "4. **Fairness and transparency are instrumented, not assumed.** Unequal outcomes enter through the corpus, prompt framing, examples and routing, which you control. Log each decision so users, regulators and your team can reconstruct it, and govern that log as a compliance-scoped store.",
     "5. **Route review by stakes, not volume.** Cost and reversibility set the stakes; calibrated confidence decides how much passes unreviewed. Choose pre-action, post-action or sampled placement, show reviewers the inputs and flag reason, and prefer plan-level and checkpoint review over per-step approval that breeds consent fatigue.",
     "6. **A compliant entry point is a prerequisite; an evidenced control set is the proof.** Turn each obligation into a control, a named owner and a living evidence artifact revalidated over time, and keep training-use and retention claims separate.",
     "Sources: https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-new-constitution ; https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/test-and-evaluate/strengthen-guardrails/mitigate-jailbreaks ; https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/test-and-evaluate/strengthen-guardrails/reduce-hallucinations ; https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/test-and-evaluate/strengthen-guardrails/increase-consistency ; https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/test-and-evaluate/strengthen-guardrails/reduce-prompt-leak ; https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/test-and-evaluate/strengthen-guardrails/handle-streaming-refusals ; https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback ; https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/handling-stop-reasons ; https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/use-case-guides/content-moderation ; https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/api-and-data-retention ; https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/data-residency ; https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/overview ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/security ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks ; https://www.anthropic.com/research/prompt-injection-defenses ; https://www.anthropic.com/research/measuring-agent-autonomy ; https://www.anthropic.com/research/trustworthy-agents ; https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/how-we-contain-claude ; https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13296973-hipaa-ready-enterprise-plans ; https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13756069-public-sector-faqs"
    ],
