    "deep": "The Usage and Cost API requires an Admin API key (or equivalent org-admin credential; workspace keys do not work), offers 1m, 1h and 1d buckets for usage, supports group-by on api_key_id, workspace_id, model, service_tier, context_window and inference_geo, and its cost report uses daily buckets. Data typically appears within about five minutes. Claude Enterprise organizations use a separate Analytics API. (Source: https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/usage-cost-api) Team and Enterprise analytics include spend over several periods and spend by model, with a CSV spend report; Enterprise Admins can view all analytics except Spend. (Source: https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12883420-view-usage-analytics-for-team-and-enterprise-plans) The Enterprise consumption guide recommends managing limits at group and user level rather than relying on the org-wide ceiling, and describes org spend alerts to admins at 75% and 90% of the org limit. (Source: https://support.claude.com/en/articles/14782391-claude-enterprise-consumption-guide)",
