    "why": "A scheduled trigger is the only kind that fires when nothing looks wrong, which is exactly when a regulator expects the record to exist anyway.",
    "why2": "Making every trigger metric-based. Compliance audits and residency confirmations are calendar-driven; tying them to thresholds means they never run while metrics look healthy.",
    "deep": "For residency rows on the direct API, the inference_geo parameter controls where inference runs ('us' or 'global', with 'global' the default unless a workspace default is set), and response.usage.inference_geo reports where inference actually ran, which makes a useful evidence artifact for a scheduled confirmation. Workspace settings can restrict allowed geos and set a default. Data at rest is governed separately by workspace geo. (Source: https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/data-residency)",
