    "id": "pf7-takeaways",
    "part": "p7-tk",
    "h": "Module key takeaways",
    "p": [
     "1. Team setup is shared configuration, distribution and spend posture decided up front. The baseline is committed project settings and CLAUDE.md under org-wide managed settings; skills reach people through org-provisioned Skills (everyone), plugins (group/org targeting with versioned updates and rollback), project Skills (one team, versioned with the repo) or API Skills (programmatic reuse); and model and budget guardrails bound it all.",
     "2. Instructions guide; configuration enforces. CLAUDE.md and skills are context Claude follows. Permissions, managed settings and hooks are what actually block. Anything with 'must', 'never' or 'cannot override' goes in settings or a hook; keep CLAUDE.md lean, specific and checkable.",
     "3. Match the permission mode to the job, and scale verification with autonomy. Manual, acceptEdits and plan for hands-on work; auto for hands-off with a classifier guarding intent; dontAsk for unattended pipelines; bypass only in isolation. The classifier never checks correctness, so diff-first review, hook-gated tests, JSON/exit-code checks and a cold second reviewer carry that load.",
     "4. Automate with the least you have to build. Routines for recurring cloud work, Code Review for managed PR review, the GitHub Action when Claude must act in CI, headless `-p` (with `--bare` for reproducibility) for your own pipelines, the Agent SDK when the agent belongs in your product.",
     "5. Steer long sessions deliberately: plan first, compact with instructions, rewind when Claude drifts, set transcript-checkable goals, poll with loops, and isolate parallel work in worktrees.",
     "6. Adoption is engineered through champions and batches; access without enablement stalls at basic chat, and lumpy adoption never standardizes the gain. Plugins carry the setup, and you read before you install because they run with your privileges.",
     "7. Diligence keeps AI-assisted work trustworthy: a verification checklist covering correctness, security, maintainability and human understanding, automated wherever possible, gating before production.",
     "8. Operational support is translation plus self-sufficiency: connect symptoms to architecture causes with evidence, instrument with OpenTelemetry and quality signals, and leave runbooks and escalation paths so the team needs you for the new problem, not the familiar one.",
     "Sources: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/overview ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/server-managed-settings ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permission-modes ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/create ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/components ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/security ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/headless ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/routines ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/scheduled-tasks ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/goal ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/checkpointing ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/worktrees ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/github-actions ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/code-review ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/costs ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/monitoring-usage ; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/overview"
    ],
