     "3. Observe before you change behavior. Add decision-level logging and expert spot-checks to learn whether escalations are justified caution or over-conservatism, and only then tune thresholds.",
     "4. Auditors need traceability, not identical outputs. When cohorts are served differently (model tier, context depth), log model version and tier per result and label lower-tier results for what they are.",
     "5. Some escalations are a format problem, not a knowledge problem. Restructure correct output for how clinicians scan it under pressure, and use HITL outcomes to measure which changes actually reduce escalations."
